# ReceiptQA: Domain VQA with a Small VLM + QLoRA

Fine-tune **SmolVLM** with **QLoRA** to answer questions about receipts, entirely on a single 8GB laptop GPU, and measure how much it beats the zero-shot base model.

> Status: 🚧 in progress. All numbers below are placeholders until evaluation is done.
> Domain is receipts (CORD). It is swappable: see `docs/DATA.md`.

## Demo

![demo](assets/demo.gif)

Live app: `<HF Spaces link>`

## Results

| Model                     | Exact Match | ANLS | Numeric Acc. | Latency (s/q) |
|---------------------------|-------------|------|--------------|---------------|
| SmolVLM-500M (zero-shot)  | TBD         | TBD  | TBD          | TBD           |
| + QLoRA (this repo)       | TBD         | TBD  | TBD          | TBD           |

Test set: 100 held-out receipts (split by receipt, not by question). 95% bootstrap CIs in `docs/EVALUATION.md`.

## Quickstart

```bash
git clone <repo> && cd receipt-vqa
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"

make data      # download CORD, build QA jsonl
make baseline  # zero-shot eval of the base model
make train     # QLoRA fine-tune (configs/train_500m_qlora.yaml)
make eval      # evaluate adapter vs base
make app       # launch Gradio demo
```

## Code status

| Part | Status |
|------|--------|
| Data builder, splits, metrics, bootstrap, error tagging | Implemented, unit-tested (`make test`) |
| Collator label masking | Pure-Python part unit-tested; full collator test needs torch |
| Model loading, QLoRA training, evaluation, Gradio app | Implemented, **not yet run on a GPU** |

First run on your machine: `make test`, `make data`, `make overfit` (loss must go to ~0), then `python scripts/token_stats.py`.
If the processor or chat template differs on your transformers version, the collator raises a clear error instead of silently mis-masking.

## Hardware

Developed on a laptop GPU with 8GB VRAM (bf16, 4-bit base weights, gradient checkpointing). Runs on any CUDA GPU with >= 8GB.

